{"id": "EUVD-2026-71421", "enisaUuid": "fb9c320c-3139-34e9-842e-7decdb300a1a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfutex/pi: Reject cross-mm private futex owners\n\nA private futex key borrows the waiter's mm without taking an mm_users\nreference. Nevertheless, attach_to_pi_owner() currently accepts an owner\nfrom a different address space and copies the private key into the owner's\nPI state.\n\nWhen that owner exits, exit_pi_state_list() uses the saved key to find the\nhash bucket and acquires a reference to the waiter's private hash. If the\nlast user of the waiter's mm exits concurrently, futex_hash_free() frees\nthe hash while the owner still uses its bucket and reference.\n\nPrevent this by validating in attach_to_pi_owner() that, for private\nfutexes, the owner mm and waiter mm are the same. Perform the check with\nthe owner's pi_lock held and after validating owner::futex::state to\nserialize against a concurrent PI-state exit cleanup.\n\n[ tglx: Amended comment ]", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:12:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:43:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b92e5562653b5293529f63b0300837d9dcedbd7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f7fb3e07752688842cbe0b85cf0d98c2fbf76b68", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43b148d796aa338858792d0167cebdc12b8cb4b9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/59b3732f95dda1fbd2234514d35f4fb6b5bb6d85"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pwhw-9cfc-qqqx", "CVE-2026-80778"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1f26e24a-9144-31e5-ab18-0e3e7bd06224", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "80367ad01d93ac781b0e1df246edaf006928002f <43b148d796aa338858792d0167cebdc12b8cb4b9"}, {"id": "49739bbf-7b72-3882-8eba-f48afebd3c3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "80367ad01d93ac781b0e1df246edaf006928002f <f7fb3e07752688842cbe0b85cf0d98c2fbf76b68"}, {"id": "5b2a88d5-11fe-3ce3-bcb7-9910bc0c49c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5bd855dc-2bc8-389e-a7a2-894f228419b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.11"}, {"id": "692bf437-1333-3be7-aa78-dea9349fec05", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "85131c2d-f88b-3e63-af27-5b1a8f655c3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "80367ad01d93ac781b0e1df246edaf006928002f <2b92e5562653b5293529f63b0300837d9dcedbd7"}, {"id": "cfc71637-dd97-35e6-b80b-faec9caa7ebc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d2b19ea6-f229-34b5-a8ba-84db1a33964e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "80367ad01d93ac781b0e1df246edaf006928002f <59b3732f95dda1fbd2234514d35f4fb6b5bb6d85"}, {"id": "d8b892f1-3603-3556-95ca-24c64d340ab0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.1"}, {"id": "e552f640-5d25-3964-bff8-9537baffae34", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.47"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3f177def-d354-318c-9a7e-2d3520d4126d", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}